{ Welcome to Chapter 2 of our White repertoire — mark this entry as Informational on Chessable.<br><br>Facing the rock-solid Nimzo-Indian 3... Bb4, we choose the classical 4. e3 Rubinstein System rather than sharp 4. Qc2 or 4. f3 mazes. It fights for central harmony, avoids early doubled-pawn compromises on our own terms, and equips you with four crystal-clear structural blueprints. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 { 3... Bb4 pins the c3 knight to our e1 king and fights directly for e4. Instead of spending a tempo on 4. Qc2 or 4. Bd2, we quietly shield c4 and open the f1-a6 diagonal with 4. e3. } { [%csl Ye3,Rc3] [%cal Bb4c3,Ge2e3] } 4. e3 { 4. e3 is our anchor move. It locks in the classical Rubinstein structure and shields c4 while opening the f1-a6 diagonal. } { [%csl Ye3] [%cal Bf1d3] } 4... O-O { 4... O-O is the classical main move. Click any of Black's four main move-4 alternatives below to see our unified map: } ( 4... c5 5. Ne2 { — Against 4... c5, 5. Ne2! avoids doubled c-pawns via a3/Nxc3 and keeps +0.28 pressure — +0.41 if Black trades 5... cxd4 6. exd4!.<br><br>What about 4... b6?: } ) ( 4... b6 5. Ne2 { — Against the St. Petersburg 4... b6, 5. Ne2! stops ...Bb7/Bxc3 structural damage and builds e4 or d5 pressure.<br><br>Against early 4... d5?: } ) ( 4... d5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 { — With Black's king still on e8, 5. a3! claims the bishop pair immediately before expanding with cxd5, Bd3, and Ne2.<br><br>And if Black captures on c3 right away?: } ) ( 4... Bxc3+ 5. bxc3 b6 6. Bd3 { — Immediate 4... Bxc3+ hands over the bishop pair without compensation — White builds f3, Ne2, and e4. } ) 5. Bd3 { After 4... O-O, 5. Bd3 eyes h7 and prepares Nf3 and O-O cleanly — scoring 52.4% online and 52.5% in Masters. } { [%csl Yd3] [%cal Bd3h7] } 5... d5 6. Nf3 { 6. Nf3 enters the Classical Gligoric tabiya. Throughout Chapter 2 you will master four reusable blueprints:<br><br>• Dynamic d4 IQP — classic isolated d4 battles after dxc4 and Bxc4, met by 10. Qe2! or Bg5, Re1, and d4-d5 breaks.<br><br>• Isolated d5 Siege — trading on d5 and c5 against ...Nc6, targeting Black's exposed d5 pawn.<br><br>• Queenside Space Clamp — c4-c5 and b2-b4 in 4... c5 and early ...c5 setups.<br><br>• Bishop Pair & e4 Steamroller — bxc3, Bd3, Ne2, and f3-e4 against early ...Bxc3+. } { [%csl Gd4,Gc4] [%cal Bf3e5,Be1g1,Bc1g5] } *

