━ PLAN FROM HERE ━━━<br><br>Verdict: +0.10 to +0.17 — Balanced Classical IQP with Active Pieces<br><br>• Our Plan — Play a3 or Rc1, swing Qd3 and Rad1, and look for Ne5 or d4-d5 once Black commits ...b6 and ...Bb7.<br><br>• Watch Out — Black wants ...a6 and ...b5 or ...b6 and ...Bb7 to control d5, or ...Nd5 to swap minor pieces; keep a3 ready against ...Nb4.<br><br>• Key Trades & Endgame — Avoid minor-piece trades while keeping the d4 IQP unless d4-d5 creates passed pawns or targets on the kingside.<br><br><br>━━━ SAMPLE CONTINUATIONS ━━━<br><br>Explore White's active IQP continuations against 11... b6 and 11... a6: } { [%csl Gd4,Ye5] [%cal Ga2a3,Gd1d3,Bf3e5,Rc6b4] } ( 11. Re1 b6 12. a3 h6 13. Bh4 Bb7 { — 12. a3 prepares Qd3 and Ba2-b1 attacks while keeping ...Nb4 out — +0.17.<br><br>If Black pushes on the queenside first with 11... a6?: } ) ( 11. Re1 a6 12. Rc1 b5 13. d5 { — Immediate 12. Rc1! meets 12... b5 with the tactical central thrust 13. d5! — +0.17. } ) *

